  "basis": "The chart's y-axis is labeled 'Number of Tourists' with an increasing scale from 0 to 3,500, and the x-axis is labeled 'Year' with ticks from 1880 to 1891. The plotted blue line, representing the new-tourist record, starts at approximately 1,100 in 1880 and ends at approximately 3,200 in 1891. Because the endpoint at the later year is significantly higher on the vertical scale than the starting point, the visual data indicates a clear increasing trend over the 1880-1891 period. Although the chart title contains the word 'Decreasing', the plotted data is the primary evidence for the trend. An increasing trend in new tourists corresponds to the 'Route to tourism growth planning' option.",
